    <bpmn:process id="W_W3431" name="W3431. Cross-Functional Account Coordination &amp; Internal Alignment" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Account need spanning functions; multi-site/multi-entity delivery
Frequency: Continuous
Volume: ~700 strategic accounts
Owner: Account Manager
Participants: Account Manager, Category (links to VS-01), Supply (links to VS-02), Project (links to VS-11.2/VS-66/VS-77), Credit (links to VS-68), Service (links to VS-12), Logistics (links to VS-06/VS-74), Store (links to VS-07)
Source: workflow W3431 — Cross-Functional Account Coordination &amp; Internal Alignment</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3431_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3431_Lane1" name="Account Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3431_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3431_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3431_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3431_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3431_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3431_Start3" name="Account need spanning functions; multi-site/multi-entity delivery">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3431_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3431_Task4" name="Account Manager act as the single throat-to-choke for the strategic account…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Account Manager act as the single throat-to-choke for the strategic account: intake needs, coordinate category/specialist engagement, resolve cross-functional conflicts (e.g., credit hold vs sales links to VS-68/VS-16), and align pricing/contract (links to W3434) and delivery (links to VS-06/VS-74/VS-77)
Responsible (R): Account Manager
Accountable (A): Head of Strategic Accounts
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3431_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3431_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3431_Task5" name="Account Manager coordinate multi-site/multi-entity delivery (e.g., a developer…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Account Manager coordinate multi-site/multi-entity delivery (e.g., a developer with projects across regions/entities per VS-72): align store/DC capacity (links to VS-07/VS-04), logistics (links to VS-06/VS-74), pricing consistency (links to VS-01.2/VS-57), and intercompany settlement (links to VS-17.2/VS-72); ensure seamless customer experience
Responsible (R): Account Manager / Operations
Accountable (A): Head of Strategic Accounts
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3431_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3431_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3431_Task6" name="Account Manager convene internal account huddles, track open issues/actions to…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Account Manager convene internal account huddles, track open issues/actions to closure, escalate blockers to the Sponsor/executives (links to VS-33.2), and capture coordination lessons to improve the account-team model (W3428)
Responsible (R): Account Manager
Accountable (A): Head of Strategic Accounts
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3431_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3431_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3431_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3431_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3431_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-550 (ensure controlled execution — Strategic Account Selection, Planning &amp; Relationship Governance (PA-107.1).) | - operational: single account owner and huddles; operational: enterprise contract governance (W3434)
Owner: Account Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W3431_Assoc9" sourceRef="W3431_Annotation8" targetRef="W3431_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W3431_Flow10" sourceRef="W3431_Start3" targetRef="W3431_Task4" />
