    <bpmn:process id="W_W3432" name="W3432. Strategic Account Compliance, Ethics &amp; Conflict-of-Interest Governance" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Account onboarding (W3426); government/regulated account; annual compliance review
Frequency: Continuous + annual
Volume: All strategic accounts; esp. government/regulated (links to VS-46/VS-86)
Owner: Head of Strategic Accounts
Participants: Head of Strategic Accounts, Compliance (links to VS-22), Legal (links to VS-100), AFC/AML (links to VS-86), Ethics/HR (links to VS-19)
Source: workflow W3432 — Strategic Account Compliance, Ethics &amp; Conflict-of-Interest Governance</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3432_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3432_Lane1" name="Compliance">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3432_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3432_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W3432_Lane2" name="Head of Strategic Accounts">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3432_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W3432_Lane3" name="Internal Audit">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3432_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3432_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3432_Start5" name="Account onboarding (W3426); government/regulated account; annual compliance review">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3432_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3432_Task6" name="Compliance/Legal screen strategic accounts for…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Compliance/Legal screen strategic accounts for regulatory/sanctions/PEP/adverse-media exposure (links to VS-86.1 KYC/CDD/PEP/sanctions), government-account eligibility (links to VS-46), anti-bribery risk (links to VS-86.3), and conflict-of-interest (e.g., account affiliated with a BuildRight executive/family); document findings
Responsible (R): Compliance / Legal / AFC
Accountable (A): Head of Strategic Accounts
Duration: Per account + annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3432_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3432_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3432_Task7" name="Head of Strategic Accounts/Compliance apply controls: enhanced due diligence…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Head of Strategic Accounts/Compliance apply controls: enhanced due diligence for high-risk accounts, gifts/entertainment approval (links to VS-86.3), government-procurement compliance (links to VS-46 PhilGEPS), anti-bribery attestations, and conflict recusal; ensure the relationship respects BuildRight ethics policy (links to VS-186) and whistleblower system (links to VS-79/W356)
Responsible (R): Head of Strategic Accounts / Compliance
Accountable (A): VP Legal / COO
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3432_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3432_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3432_Task8" name="Internal Audit/Compliance review strategic-account compliance periodically…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Internal Audit/Compliance review strategic-account compliance periodically (links to VS-21), investigate alerts, and report material issues to executives/Audit Committee (links to VS-36); ensure data-privacy compliance for account data (links to VS-91)
Responsible (R): Internal Audit / Compliance
Accountable (A): Audit Committee
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3432_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3432_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3432_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3432_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3432_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-87 (ensure key-account credit concentration &amp; ethics governance.) | - operational: anti-bribery controls (links to VS-86); operational: COI screening and recusal
Owner: Head of Strategic Accounts</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
